\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10512\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2025 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2025 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 8/11: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XRP, DOGE, DOT, UNI, LINK, SOL\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,878 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 August 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and most major altcoins remain above their respective 200-day moving average but the market's momentum will depend on whether BTC can pierce the $48,000 level.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) strong recovery and march toward the psychological level at $50,000 has improved the overall sentiment in the crypto sector. That has boosted the total {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/total-crypto-market-value-breaks-1-9t-for-first-time-since-may"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto market capitalization to over $1.9 trillion}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Data from Glassnode shows a sharp increase in the dominance of Bitcoin transactions exceeding $1 million in the past few months. The on-chain analytics firm noted in its report that the transactions by the $1 million to $10 million group surged when Bitcoin corrected to $29,000 in July. This suggests that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/large-hodlers-accumulate-bitcoin-below-50k-as-btc-transactions-over-1m-soar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 institutional investors may have been buyi}}}\uc2  ng, which is \u8220\'20\'1Cfairly constructive for price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/2bb12b9a-0b51-4ce5-b8aa-38717c7dfde7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Further evidence of possible institutional buying came from CryptoQuant data showing that Bitcoin reserves on derivatives exchanges have declined to 1.256 million Bitcoin, the lowest level since May 11. A similar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutions-are-buying-bitcoin-like-it-s-late-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drop in derivatives exchange balances}}}\uc2  was seen before the start of the bull run at the end of 2020.\par \par \uc2 With signs of institutional accumulation increasing, could the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum pick up further in the next few days or is it high time to book profits? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears have been attempting to pull the price back below the 200-day simple moving average ($45,091) for the past two days but the bulls have held their ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/6bac73c2-8963-4846-8ec4-9a33d7605275.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average ($41,010) has been sloping up and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the overbought zone, indicating that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 If buyers propel the price above $46,700, the BTC/USDT pair is likely to start its journey toward the $50,000 to $51,500 resistance zone. The bears will try to stall the rally in this zone but if the bulls can overcome the challenge, the pair could rise to $60,000.\par \par \uc2 If bears pull the price back below the 200-day SMA, the pair could drop to the 20-day EMA. If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will make another attempt to start the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, a break below the 20-day EMA could open the doors for a decline to the next support at $36,670. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because if it cracks, the bears will smell an opportunity.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) strong rebound on Aug. 9 shows that bulls flipped the $3,000 level into support. This level is likely to act as a floor on future declines.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/bf11e391-0442-41cd-a67a-e5e9856559e1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ETHUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to resume the uptrend today. The ETH/USDT pair could now rally to the $3,4441.73 to $3,587.06 resistance zone where the bears are likely to pose a stiff challenge.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from this zone but rebounds off $3,000, it will suggest that bulls are buying on dips. That will improve the prospects of a rally to $4,000.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if bears pull the price below the 20-day EMA ($2,712), it will suggest that the current breakout was a bull trap. The pair could then drop to the 200-day SMA ($2,229).\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the moving averages on Aug. 9 and started its upward journey toward the resistance of the large $211.70 to $433 range. The bears are likely to defend the $433 level aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/c912a192-7597-43a3-af44-8df609615a30.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BNBUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, if bulls do not give up much ground near $433 or if they buy the dips to the 20-day EMA ($338), the likelihood of a break above $433 increases. If that happens, the BNB/USDT pair could rally to $520 and later to $600.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance and breaks below $340, it will suggest that the range-bound action may continue for a few more days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears attempted to stall Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) relief rally at the $1.50 resistance but they could not pull the price back below the 20-day EMA ($1.42). This showed that bulls were not booking profits as they anticipated the recovery to continue.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/56d8b9ac-60c6-4bdb-931e-200f0066cfcc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair surged above the $1.50 level on Aug. 10 and could now rally to the overhead resistance at $1.94. This level could attract profit-booking and if the price turns down from it, the bears will attempt to pull the price back to $1.50.\par \par \uc2 If that happens, the pair could extend its range-bound action for a few more days. On the contrary, if bulls thrust the price above $1.94, the pair could challenge the all-time high at $2.47. A breakout and close above this level will suggest the resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls successfully held the retest of the breakout level at $0.75 on Aug. 9 and pushed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/ripple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  back above the 200-day SMA ($0.80). The altcoin could now rally to the downtrend line of the descending channel where the bears may mount a stiff resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/c98ac518-6cb9-427d-82f7-e99c34a8d3d2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/XRPUSD/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the downtrend line but rebounds off the 20-day EMA ($0.75), it will indicate that bulls are buying on dips. A breakout and close above the descending channel will signal a possible change in trend.\par \par \uc2 The first target on the upside is $1.07 and if bulls push the price above this resistance, the up-move may reach $1.26. Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level or the downtrend line and breaks below $0.69, it will suggest that the downtrend remains intact.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $0.29 on Aug. 8 but the correction was short-lived as the price again bounced back on Aug. 9. The bulls will now try to push the price above the overhead resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/3660c273-6cad-450f-a260-60faae09fb74.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOGEUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the DOGE/USDT pair could rally to $0.35. This level may act as stiff resistance but if bulls clear this hurdle, the up-move may reach $0.45. The 20-day EMA ($0.22) has started to turn up and the RSI is just below the overbought zone, suggesting that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from $0.29, the pair could drop to the 20-day EMA. If the price rebounds off this support, the bulls will make one more attempt to propel the price above $0.29. Conversely, a break below the 20-day EMA could keep the pair range-bound between $0.21 and $0.29 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears attempted to stall Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) recovery at the overhead resistance at $21 for the past few days but the bulls did not give up much ground. This suggests that bulls are buying on every minor dip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/49bbf10e-d8eb-4f6d-afd4-568cfc37f583.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/DOTUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The rising 20-day EMA ($18.18) and the RSI in the overbought zone suggest that bulls are in control. If buyers sustain the price above $21, the DOT/USDT pair could start its journey to the overhead resistance at $26.50.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from $26.50, the pair could drop to $21 and remain range-bound between these two levels. A breakout and close above $26.50 will suggest the start of a new uptrend that may reach $31.28. The bears will have to pull the price back below $16.93 to tilt the advantage in their favor.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/uniswap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UNI}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $30 on Aug. 10 but the bears have not been able to sustain the lower levels. This suggests that bulls are buying on every minor dip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/860f8339-1978-4cb8-b5f3-febed0295469.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/UNIUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If bulls push and close the price above $30, the UNI/USDT pair could start its northward march toward $37. A breakout of this resistance could clear the path for a retest of the all-time high at $45.\par \par \uc2 However, the RSI is in the overbought territory suggests that the rally could be overextended in the short term. That may result in a pullback to the 200-day SMA ($26). A strong bounce off this support will suggest that bulls are in command. The bears will have to pull and sustain the price below $23.45 to gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-dollar-downturn-aids-bitcoin-bulls-before-50k-btc-price-showdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US dollar downturn aids Bitcoin bulls before $50K BTC price showdown}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USDT\par \par \uc2 The relief rally in Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/chainlink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) has reached the critical overhead resistance zone at $26.48 and the 200-day SMA ($27.86) where the bears are likely to pose a stiff challenge.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/63b5c2e7-1258-4ac6-bd43-b1cdfc63d86e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/LINKUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from this zone, the LINK/USDT pair could again drop to the 20-day EMA ($22.37). A strong rebound off this support will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and the bulls will then make one more attempt to clear the overhead hurdle.\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close above the 200-day SMA will suggest that bears have lost their grip. The pair could then rise to $32 and later to $35.33. Conversely, a break and close below the $22.07 support will suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has weakened.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bears to sustain Solana (SOL) below $38.10 on Aug. 9 attracted further buying, which has pushed the price to the overhead resistance at $44.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/c28bcef8-8862-4003-861d-1900541b75ae.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/SOLUSDT/?utm_source=cointelegraph&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_campaign=news&utm_term=btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 If bulls thrust the price above $44, the SOL/USDT pair could rally to the psychological resistance at $50 and then retest the all-time high at $58.38. A breakout and close above this resistance will signal the resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA ($35.59) and the RSI in the overbought territory suggest that bulls have the upper hand. This positive view will invalidate if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the 20-day EMA. That could pull the price down to $32 and then to the 200-day SMA ($26.81).\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDgvNTIwNzQ4YWEtNzYzYi00MTZiLTg0ZTUtNTYwODMxNTNhMjQwLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210811eh8b000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cardano\par \b \uc2 Cardano faces $1.60 resistance after  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2  price hits 2-month highs\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 452 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cardano price action focuses on $1.60 resistance after 2-month highs for \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  token came close to its highest in two months on Aug. 10 as daily gains neared 6%.\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.45454375.247013567.1628609843-318021975.1628081796"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ADAUSD/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  showed \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD challenging resistance to reach $1.59 \u8212\'20\'14 its highest since June 15.\par \par \uc2 Cardano bulls battle $1.60\par \par \uc2 One of the top performers in the top fifty cryptocurrencies by market cap, Cardano was yet to overcome multi-month resistance at around $1.60 at the time of writing.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, performance was impressive, catching the attention of veteran trader Peter Brandt who keenly eyed recent strength.\par \par \uc2 "New development in Cardano ADAUSD. The advance through the July 4 high goes a long way to negate the potential bearishness of the H&S top in this crypto," he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeterLBrandt/status/1425077211573403660"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2 Twitter\uc2  followers in an update on the day.\par \par \uc2 "In fact, this price action can be viewed as \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as price remains above 1.25."{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeterLBrandt/status/1425077211573403660/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/PeterLBrandt/status/1425077211573403660/photo/1}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/ad074d1c-b8b9-4f8c-b02d-9dda95b50469.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD 1-day candle chart (Binance). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Brandt referred to a recent head & shoulders construction on \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD, which the run to the highs of Aug. 10 had helped overcome.\par \par \uc2 Fellow trader and Cointelegraph contributor Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe was similarly upbeat on the future price odds.\par \par \uc2 "Good bounce of Cardano, but didn't break the downtrend yet. Looks good," he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1425114754637500416"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 summarized}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1425114754637500416/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1425114754637500416/photo/1}}}\par \par \uc2 Against Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  put in a strong return after looking for a retest of support, Van de Poppe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1424905839232552961"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Monday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/f022fa6e-7079-4ce2-8237-01e70f589a66.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BTC 1-day candle chart (Binance). Source: TradingView\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD saw its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-smashes-2-resistance-as-bullish-signals-enter-for-bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all-time highs}}}\uc2  of $2.50 on May 16, coinciding with a turning point across altcoins as Bitcoin fell due to the China-inspired miner exodus and the associated loss of hash rate.\par \par \uc2 Altcoins enjoy Bitcoin beating gains\par \par \uc2 On weekly timeframes, many altcoins outperformed Bitcoin's 18.5% gains, boosted by Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) in the aftermath of its successful {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-london-hard-fork-goes-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 London hard fork deployment}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-8-9-btc-eth-bnb-ada-xrp-doge-dot-uni-bch-link"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 8/9: BTC, ETH, BNB, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , XRP, DOGE, DOT, UNI, BCH, LINK}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD stood at $3,110 at the time of writing, up 25% versus seven days ago and fresh off local highs of nearly $3,200.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-08/c8281980-20df-4c58-b6e2-1f8eab5ec2b1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD 1-day candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 As Cointelegraph noted, the total cryptocurrency market cap {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/total-crypto-market-value-breaks-1-9t-for-first-time-since-may"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed $1.9 trillion for the first time}}}\uc2  this week since May, nearing the significant $2 trillion mark once again.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDgvNzJiOWU1ZGMtMGY5ZC00ZTViLThhYTctNDMxYWJiNzAwY2RiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210810eh8a000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin investment products still suffering outflows despite price recovery\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Martin Young \par \uc2 455 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  has reported a fifth consecutive week of net withdrawals from institutional crypto products.\par \par \uc2 Institutional crypto products have seen their fifth consecutive week of outflows despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum in the markets.\par \par \uc2 In its Monday \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinshares.com/research/digital-asset-fund-flows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , institutional asset manager \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  estimated that outflows totaled $26 million for the week. However, the report notes that outflows have shrunk compared to May and June when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/record-141m-outflow-from-bitcoin-products-signals-institutions-are-bearish-on-btc-coinshares"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outflows surged to a record $141 million per week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) gaining 17.5% over the past week, Bitcoin funds shed $33 million during the same period.\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 own BTC product was the biggest loser for the period with an outflow of $63.3 million, while the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest crypto asset manager, Grayscale, remained flat. According to Grayscale\u8217\'20\'19s latest update on Tuesday, the combined value of assets managed by its funds has climbed back above $40 billion for the first time since mid-May.\par \par \uc2 08/09/21 UPDATE: Net Assets Under Management, Holdings per Share, and Market Price per Share for our Investment Products.\par \par \uc2 Total AUM: $40.4 billion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BAT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BAT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BCH&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BCH}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LINK&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LINK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24MANA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $MANA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ETH&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETH}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ETC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24FIL&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $FIL}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ZEN&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ZEN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LPT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LPT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24XLM&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $XLM}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ZEC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ZEC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24UNI&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $UNI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24AAVE&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $AAVE}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24COMP&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $COMP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24CRV&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $CRV}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24MKR&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $MKR}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24SUSHI&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $SUSHI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24SNX&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $SNX}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24YFI&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $YFI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24UMA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $UMA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BNT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BNT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ADA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ju95J9n68H"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ju95J9n68H}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Grayscale (@Grayscale) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Grayscale/status/1424834520512139270?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 However, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-investment-products-see-largest-weekly-outflows-on-record-coinshares"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ether-based investment products}}}\uc2  saw inflows of $2.8 million for the week as Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) rallied after last week\u8217\'20\'19s successful London upgrades. Ether products now represent 26% of capital invested into institutional crypto products.\par \par \uc2 There were minor inflows for some altcoin funds, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2 , Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and multi-asset funds, each of which saw inflows of between $1.1 million and $800,000.\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  also noted that 2021 has already seen a record 37 new crypto funds launched so far, beating out the 30 cryptocurrency funds that were launched during 2018:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have seen the number of funds/investment products listed accelerate recently with a record 37 launched this year compared to the previous high of 30 seen in 2018.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bears-lick-their-paws-while-bitcoin-price-blasts-through-46-000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent market momentum}}}\uc2 , the combined assets under management (AUM) of all institutional crypto products have surpassed $50 billion \u8212\'20\'14 its highest level since mid-May.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutions-continue-offloading-btc-exposure-despite-price-rebound"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Institutions continue offloading BTC exposure despite price rebound}}}\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinshares.com/investor-relations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  its financials for the first half of 2021, revealing a total income of $81.2 million. As such, \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  has already tripled what it earned for the entirety of 2020 during the first half of this year.\par \par \uc2 As of June 30, 2021, \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 total AUM was $3 billion, up 27.6% compared to the end of December 2020.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDgvYjlmZDVmZjItY2Y3Zi00NzI1LWE0ZmUtODA2MmViMDRjOWZlLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210810eh8a0005q\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin investment products still suffering outflows despite price recovery\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Martin Young \par \uc2 452 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  has reported a fifth consecutive week of net withdrawals from institutional crypto products.\par \par \uc2 Institutional crypto products have seen their fifth consecutive week of outflows despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum in the markets.\par \par \uc2 In its August 9 \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinshares.com/research/digital-asset-fund-flows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , institutional asset manager \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  estimated that outflows totaled $26 million for the week. However, the report notes that outflows have shrunk compared to during May and June, when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/record-141m-outflow-from-bitcoin-products-signals-institutions-are-bearish-on-btc-coinshares"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outflows surged to a record $141 million per week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite BTC gaining 17.5% over the past week, Bitcoin funds shed $33 million this past week.\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 own BTC product was the biggest loser for the period with an outflow of $63.3 million while the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest crypto asset manager, Grayscale, remained flat. According to Grayscale\u8217\'20\'19s latest update on August 10, the combined value of assets managed by its funds has climbed back above $40 billion for the first time since mid-May.\par \par \uc2 08/09/21 UPDATE: Net Assets Under Management, Holdings per Share, and Market Price per Share for our Investment Products.\par \par \uc2 Total AUM: $40.4 billion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BAT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BAT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BCH&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BCH}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LINK&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LINK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24MANA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $MANA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ETH&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETH}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ETC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24FIL&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $FIL}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ZEN&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ZEN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LPT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LPT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24XLM&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $XLM}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%